---
description: WebMCP implementation rules
alwaysApply: true
---
- Use the current WebMCP specification as the source of truth.
- Current target APIs include document.modelContext.registerTool(), getTools(), and executeTool().
- Keep compatibility code isolated.
- Every tool needs typed schema, side-effect classification, deterministic result/error contract, authorization expectations and idempotency behavior when mutating.
- A provider tool must cause/observe real provider state.
- Re-read provider state after consequential mutation.
